  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures the Mountain Goats performing at The Queen in Wilmington, Delaware, on Saturday, December 2, 2023 [1]. The setlist includes thirty-seven tracks, spanning a total duration of one hundred and eleven minutes [1]. The performance features the song \"Jenny III\" alongside \"Murder At The 18th St. Garage\" and \"Dark In Here\" [1]. A notable highlight is the saxophone introduction to \"Guys On Every Corner,\" which is the only archived performance of that specific segment [1]. The band also plays \"Fresh Tattoo,\" \"Night Light,\" and \"Blood Capsules,\" the latter being a bustout that had not appeared in the previous ninety-nine archived shows [1]. Following a solo set transition, the group performs \"Song For An Old Friend\" and \"Alpha Omega\" [1]. The set continues with \"Pseudothyrum Song,\" \"Cleaning Crew,\" and \"Only One Way\" [1]. Later in the show, the band plays \"Jeff Davis County Blues,\" \"Cotton,\" and \"Clean Slate\" [1]. The performance concludes with \"This Year,\" \"The Diaz Brothers,\" and \"Before I Got There\" [1]. The final songs include \"First Blood,\" \"You Or Your Memory,\" \"Up The Wolves,\" and \"No Children\" [1]. A bonus round features \"Amy AKA Spent Gladiator 1\" and \"Heel Turn 2\" [1]. This is the three hundred and ninety-fifth show in the archive's collection for the performer [2]. The previous archived show took place at The Rialto on November 25, 2023 [2]. The recording was taped by n3t_Rchae010gy [1].",
   "citations": [
